AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003204> "\"Eating one of these small bananas (about 100 g) covers the vitamin A requirement for 2 days. The Cavendish variety, on the other hand, contains almost no vitamin A. Growing vitamin A-rich banana varieties in more countries could contribute to a decline in global vitamin A deficiency.\" [http://www.fao.org/zhc/detail-events/en/c/446573/]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003204> "utin lap plant"@en)
