# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> (food calorie datum)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> "A datum, measured in food calories, representing a potential amount of energy available in a food material to a consumer."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8844-9165>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calorie>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> "2020-04-12T06:54:43Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> "1 kilocalorie (kcal) = 1000 calories (cal). By convention in food science, the large calorie is commonly called calorie (with a capital C by some authors) to distinguish from the smaller unit."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003339> "food calorie datum"@en)
