# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> (rice plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "Oryza sativa, commonly known as Asian rice, is the plant species most commonly referred to in English as rice.  *Oryza sativa* contains two major subspecies: the sticky, short-grained *japonica* or *sinica* variety, and the nonsticky, long-grained *indica* variety."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> <http://eol.org/pages/1115098>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?26077>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=41976>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1322>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "MANSFELD:20986")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "PLANTS:ORSA")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "lowland rice"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "upland rice"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "Rice occurs in a variety of colors, including white, brown, black, purple, and red rices. Black rice (also known as purple rice) is a range of rice types, some of which are glutinous rice. Varieties include Indonesian black rice and Thai jasmine black rice."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411322> "rice plant"@en)
