AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411556> "Cinnamomum burmannii, also known as Indonesian cinnamon, Padang cassia, Batavia cassia, or korintje, is one of several plants in the genus *Cinnamomum* whose bark is sold as the spice cinnamon. The most common and cheapest type of cinnamon in the US is made from powdered *C. burmannii*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_burmannii]"@en)
