# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> (apple banana plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> "Latundan bananas (also called Tundan, Silk bananas, Pisang raja sereh, Manzana bananas or Apple bananas), are triploid hybrid banana cultivars from the Philippines. It is one of the most common banana cultivars in the Philippines, along with the Lacatan and Saba bananas."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> "WIKIPEDIA:Apple_Banana")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1568>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> "apple banana plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411568> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_4640>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> (atheriniform fish)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> "The Atheriniformes, also known as the silversides, are an order of ray-finned fishes that includes the Old World silversides and several less-familiar families, including the unusual *Phallostethidae*. The order includes at least 354 species. They are found worldwide in tropical and temperate marine and freshwater environments. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atheriniformes]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> <http://eol.org/pages/8268>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1573>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> "atheriniformes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> "atheriniform fish"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411573> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411365>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> (anguilliform fish)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> "An eel is any fish belonging to the order Anguilliformes, which consists of four suborders, 20 families, 111 genera and about 800 species. Most eels are predators. The term \"eel\" (originally referring to the European eel) is also used for some other similarly shaped fish, such as electric eels and spiny eels, but these are not members of the Anguilliformes order. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eel]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> <http://eol.org/pages/8280>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1574>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> "anguilliformes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> "anguilliform fish"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411574> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411365>)

