# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> (clementine plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> "A clementine (*Citrus × clementina*) is a tangor, a hybrid between a willowleaf mandarin orange (*C. × deliciosa*) and a sweet orange (*C. × sinensis*), so named in 1902. The exterior is a deep orange colour with a smooth, glossy appearance. Clementines can be separated into 7 to 14 segments. Similar to tangerines, they tend to be easy to peel. They are typically juicy and sweet, with less acid than oranges. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clementine]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> <http://eol.org/pages/4414>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?314344>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1751>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> "Citrus clementina hort. ex Tanaka")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> "citrus clementina"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> "citrus reticulata cv. clementine"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> "clementine plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411751> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411139>)

