# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> (sucker family)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> "The *Catostomidae* are the suckers of the order Cypriniformes, with about 78 species in this family of freshwater fishes. The *Catostomidae* are primarily native to North America, but *Catostomus catostomus* is found in both North America and Russia, and *Myxocyprinus asiaticus* is from China.. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catostomidae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> <http://eol.org/pages/3196>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1892>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> "catostomidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> "sucker family"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411892> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411594>)

