# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> (north american cantaloupe plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> "The North American cantaloupe, common in the United States, Mexico, and in some parts of Canada, has a net-like (or reticulated) skin covering. It is a round melon with firm, orange, moderately sweet flesh and a thin, reticulated, light-brown rind. Varieties with redder and yellower flesh exist but are not common in the U.S. market."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> "WIKIPEDIA:Cantaloupe")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4222>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> "north american cantaloupe plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414222> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414221>)

