# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414334> (greater plantain plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414334> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414334> "Plantago major (\"broadleaf plantain\" or \"greater plantain\") is a species of *Plantago*, family *Plantaginaceae*. The plant is native to most of Europe and northern and central Asia, but has widely naturalised elsewhere in the world. 
 *Plantago major* is one of the most abundant and widely distributed medicinal crops in the world. A poultice of the leaves can be applied to wounds, stings, and sores in order to facilitate healing and prevent infection."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414334> "WIKIPEDIA:Plantago_major")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414334> <http://eol.org/pages/579221>)
