AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414659> "Cassytha is a genus of some two dozen species of obligately parasitic vines in the family *Lauraceae*. The fruit of various species are eaten, both by birds and by humans, and *Cassytha melantha* in particular has been documented as a wild-harvested Australian indigenous food. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassytha]"@en)
