# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> (peanut tree)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> "Sterculia quadrifida, also known as the peanut tree, or red-fruited kurrajong is a small tree that grows in the rainforests, vine thickets and gallery forests of coastal Queensland, the Northern Territory and north-eastern New South Wales. Seed pods contain up to 8 black seeds that are edible and taste like raw peanuts. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sterculia_quadrifida]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> <http://eol.org/pages/4321>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?101919>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4682>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> "Sterculia quadrifida R. Br.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> "red-fruit kurrajong"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414682> "sterculia quadrifida"@en)
