AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414691> "Mistletoe is the most common name for most obligate hemiparasitic plants in the order *Santalales*. Mistletoes attach to and penetrate the branches of a tree or shrub by a structure called the haustorium, through which they absorb water and nutrients from the host plant.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistletoe]"@en)
