# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> (greenhood orchid plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> "Pterostylis is a genus of about 120 species of plants in the orchid family, *Orchidaceae*. Commonly called greenhood orchids, they are terrestrial, deciduous, perennial, tuberous, herbs found in Australia, New Zealand, New Guinea, New Caledonia and one Indonesian island. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterostylis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> <http://eol.org/pages/8156>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4735>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> "pterostylis spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> "greenhood orchid plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414735> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414730>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> (lovegrass plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> "Eragrostis is large and widespread genus of plants in the grass family, found in many countries on all inhabited continents and many islands. *Eragrostis* is commonly known as lovegrass or canegrass. Lovegrass is commonly used as livestock fodder. The seeds appear to be of high nutritional value for some animals, but they are also very tiny and collecting them for human food is cumbersome and hence uncommon. A notable exception is teff (*Eragrostis tef*), which is used to make traditional breads on the Horn of Africa. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eragrostis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> <http://eol.org/pages/108048>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4736>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> "canegrass"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> "eragrostid spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> "lovegrass plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414736> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03413378>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> (signalgrass plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> "Brachiaria, or signalgrass, is a genus of plants in the grass family native to tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, Africa, Australia, southern Europe, the Americas, and various islands. There are over 100 species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brachiaria]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> <http://eol.org/pages/108119>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4737>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414737> "brachiaria spp."@en)
