# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> (solanaceae plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> "The *Solanaceae*, or nightshades, are an economically important family of flowering plants. Many members of the family contain potent alkaloids, and some are highly toxic, but many, including tomatoes, potatoes, eggplant, bell/chili peppers, and tobacco are widely used. The *Solanaceae* consists of about 98 genera and some 2,700 species, with a great diversity of habitats, morphology and ecology. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanaceae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> <http://eol.org/pages/4437>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4934>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> "nightshade family"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> "solanaceae plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414934> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03413357>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> (armenian cucumber plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "The Armenian cucumber, *Cucumis melo* var. *flexuosus*, is a type of long, slender fruit which tastes like a cucumber and looks somewhat like a cucumber inside. It is actually a variety of muskmelon (*C. melo*), a species closely related to the cucumber (*C. sativus*). It is also known as the yard-long cucumber, snake cucumber, snake melon, and uri in Japan. It should not be confused with the snake gourds (*Trichosanthes* spp.). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_cucumber]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?12569>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4935>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "Cucumis melo var. flexuosus (L.) Naudin")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "cucumis melo flexuosus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "serpent melon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "snake melon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> "armenian cucumber plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414935> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414459>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> (tuberous-root mustard plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> "This mustard relative develops a tuberous root, in appearance much like a globular turnip. Roots reach a diameter of 3 to 4 inches, and are similar to turnips in appearance, texture, flavor and culture. It is rarely grown in the U.S. The root, leaves and petioles are edible. [https://dev.hort.purdue.edu/newcrop/Crops/MustardTuberousRootedChine.html]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?461021>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4941>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> "Brassica juncea subsp. napiformis (Pailleux & Bois) Gladis")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> "brassica juncea napiformis"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> "turnip-root mustard"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> "tuberous-root mustard plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414941> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411092>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> (broccolini plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> "Broccolini is a green vegetable similar to broccoli but with smaller florets and longer, thin stalks. It is a natural hybrid of broccoli and gai lan, both cultivar groups of *Brassica oleracea*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broccolini]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4945>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> "bimi"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> "broccolini plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414945> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411443>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> (batavia lettuce plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> "A lettuce which is midway between the crisphead and leaf types. These lettuces tend to be larger, bolt-resistant and well-flavored."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lettuce#Cultivars>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4946>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> "French crisp"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> "summercrisp lettuce"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> "batavia lettuce plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414946> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411390>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414951> (chokeberry plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414951> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414951> "Aronia is a genus of deciduous shrubs, the chokeberries, in the family *Rosaceae* native to eastern North America and most commonly found in wet woods and swamps. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aronia]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414951> <http://eol.org/pages/8097>)
