AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415009> "Clinopodium nepeta (synonym *Calamintha nepeta*), known as lesser calamint, is a perennial herb of the mint family. Lesser calamint is used in borders. It is also as a spice in the Italian cuisine where it is called *mentuccia, nipitella* or *nepitella*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinopodium_nepeta]"@en)
