# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> (schisandra plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> "Schisandra (magnolia vine) is a genus of twining shrubnative to East Asia, and its dried fruit is sometimes used medicinally. The berries of *S. chinensis* are given the name wu wei zi in Chinese, which translates as \"five flavor fruit\" because they possess all five basic flavors in Chinese herbal medicine: salty, sweet, sour, pungent (spicy), and bitter.  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schisandra]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> <http://eol.org/pages/4297>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?413956>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5055>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415055> "PLANTS:SCHIS2")
