# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> (pine family)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> "The *Pinaceae* (pine family) are trees or shrubs, including many of the well-known conifers of commercial importance such as cedars, firs, hemlocks, larches, pines and spruces. The family is included in the order Pinales, formerly known as Coniferales. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinaceae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> <http://eol.org/pages/6747>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5094>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> "pinaceae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> "pine family"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415094> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03413357>)

