# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> (european goldenrod plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> "Solidago virgaurea (European goldenrod or woundwort) is an herbaceous perennial plant of the family *Asteraceae*. This plant was cultivated in the Arab world, who used it in their medical system. In the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries it was used in Europe to heal wounds. It has astringent, diuretic, antiseptic and other properties. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solidago_virgaurea]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?34927>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5173>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> "Solidago virgaurea L.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> "solidago virgaurea"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> "european goldenrod plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415173> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03413359>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> (uzazi fruit)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> "The term Uziza refers to the dried fruit of the West African deciduous shrub *Zanthoxylum tessmannii* (syn.), syn. *Fagara tessmannii*, a member of the 'prickly ash' *Zanthoxylum* family. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uzazi] 
 *Zanthoxylum gilletii*, the East African satin wood, is a tree species in the genus *Zanthoxylum* found in Africa. The fruits are used to produce the spice uzazi. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanthoxylum_gilletii]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> <http://eol.org/pages/4414>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5174>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> "fagara tessmannii"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> "zanthoxylum gilletii"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> "zanthoxylum tessmannii"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> "uzazi fruit"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415174> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03412295>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> (chinese white pear plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> "Pyrus × bretschneideri (or *Pyrus ×bretschneideri*), the ya pear or pearple or Chinese white pear, is an interspecific hybrid species of pear native to North China, where it is widely grown for its edible fruit. 
 Along with cultivars of *P. pyrifolia* and *P. ussuriensis*, the fruit is also called the nashi pear. These very juicy, white to light yellow pears, unlike the round Nashi pears (*P. pyrifolia*) that are also grown in eastern Asia, are shaped more like the European pear (*Pyrus communis*), narrow towards the stem end. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrus_×_bretschneideri]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?30462>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5175>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> "Pyrus x bretschneideri Rehder")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> "pyrus x bretschneideri"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> "ya pear"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> "chinese white pear plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411344>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> (dracontomelon plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> "Dracontomelon is a genus of flowering plants in the family *Anacardiaceae*. The most commonly eaten species is *Dracontomelon duperreanum*, which produces an edible fruit that is eaten in Cambodia, Vietnam and China. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dracontomelon]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> <http://eol.org/pages/61091>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5176>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> "dracontomelon spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> "dracontomelon plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415176> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03413387>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> (actinidia plant)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "A plant of the genus Actinidia."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> <http://eol.org/pages/49128>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B5177>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "MANSFELD:26714")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "actinidia spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "kiwifruit"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "\"The fruit is a large berry containing numerous small seeds; in most species, the fruit is edible. In particular, this genus is known for the species *Actinidia deliciosa*, the kiwifruit or Chinese gooseberry, and for the hardy ornamental Actinidia kolomikta. [...] 
Kiwifruit (often abbreviated as kiwi) or Chinese gooseberry is the edible berry of several species of woody vines in the genus *Actinidia*. The most common cultivar group of kiwifruit is oval, about the size of a large hen's egg. It has a fibrous, dull greenish-brown skin and bright green or golden flesh with rows of tiny, black, edible seeds. [...] 
The most common kiwifruit is the fuzzy kiwifruit, from the species *Actinidia deliciosa*. Other species that are commonly eaten include golden kiwifruit (*Actinidia chinensis*), Chinese egg gooseberry (*Actinidia coriacea*), hardy kiwifruit (*Actinidia arguta*), Arctic kiwifruit (*Actinidia kolomikta*), purple kiwifruit (*Actinidia melanandra*), silver vine (*Actinidia polygama*), hearty red kiwifruit (*Actinidia purpurea*).\" - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiwifruit"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> "actinidia plant"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03415177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411231>)

