# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> (divided or disintegrated)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0122>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> "LanguaL curation note: The distinctions in this category are based on size characteristics, primarily thickness, which are important for heat transfer and for diffusion of chemicals in processing. *DIVIDED INTO HALVES, QUARTERS OR SEGMENTS* should be examined first and if one of the descriptors listed applies it should be used regardless of the size of the pieces. If none of these are applicable, other *DIVIDED OR DISINTEGRATED* descriptors should be examined. Do not use any of these descriptors if dividing or disintegrating results in a semiliquid or semisolid product."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> "divided or disintegrated"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430123> (food (liquid, low viscosity, with no visible particles))

