AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1071199> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1071199> "*Pterocarpus santalinus*, with the common names red sanders, red sandalwood, and saunderswood, is a species of *Pterocarpus* endemic to the southern Eastern Ghats mountain range of South India. The tree is not to be confused with the aromatic *Santalum* sandalwood trees that grow natively in South India. *Pterocarpus santalinus* is used in traditional herbal medicine [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterocarpus_santalinus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1071199> "red sandalwood plant"@en)
