# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> (Selenicereus megalanthus)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> "*Hylocereus megalanthus* is a cactus species in the genus *Hylocereus* that is native to northern South America, where it is known, along with its fruit, by the name of Pitahaya. The yellow fruit has thorns, unlike the red dragon fruits (*H. undatus, H. polyrhizus, H. costaricensis*), and is commonly known as \"yellow dragon fruit\", \"yellow pitahaya\" or \"yellow pitaya\". [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hylocereus_megalanthus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> "2023-06-19T01:50:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> "Hylocereus megalanthus (K. Schum. ex Vaupel) Ralf Bauer")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> "Hylocereus megalanthus"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1195127> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03412781>)

