AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_16752> "*Houttuynia cordata*, known as fish mint, fish leaf, lizard tail, chameleon plant, heartleaf, fishwort, and bishop's weed, is one of two species in the genus *Houttuynia* (the other being *H. emeiensis*), a flowering plant native to Japan, Korea, southern China, and Southeast Asia, where it grows in moist, shady places. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houttuynia_cordata]"@en)
