# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_169607> (Tagetes minuta)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_169607> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_169607> "*Tagetes minuta* - muster John Henry, southern marigold, Khakibos , stinking roger, wild marigold, or black mint, is a tall upright marigold plant from the genus *Tagetes*, with small flowers, native to the southern half of South America. It is used as a culinary herb in Peru, Ecuador, and parts of Chile and Bolivia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagetes_minuta]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_169607> "muster john henry plant"@en)
