# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_35874> (Dioscorea bulbifera)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_35874> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_35874> "*Dioscorea bulbifera*, the air potato, is a species of true yam in the yam family, *Dioscoreaceae*. It is native to Africa, southern Asia, India, Maldives, China, Japan, the Philippines, and Indonesia and northern Australia. The air potato is one of the most widely consumed yam species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_bulbifera]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_35874> "air potato plant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_35874> <http://eol.org/pages/1121145>)
