AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_3888> "Green \"garden\" peas, eaten immature and fresh, were an innovative luxury of Early Modern Europe. In England, the distinction between \"field peas\" and \"garden peas\" dates from the early 17th century."@en)
