# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_52969> (Ascophyllum nodosum)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_52969> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_52969> "Ascophyllum nodosum is a large, common brown alga (*Phaeophyceae*) in the family *Fucaceae*, being the only species in the genus *Ascophyllum*. It is seaweed of the northern Atlantic Ocean, also known as rockweed, Norwegian kelp, knotted kelp, knotted wrack or egg wrack. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascophyllu]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_52969> "north atlantic rockweed"@en)
