# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_57917> (Filipendula ulmaria)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_57917> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_57917> "*Filipendula ulmaria*, commonly known as meadowsweet or mead wort, is a perennial herb in the family *Rosaceae* that grows in damp meadows. Meadowsweet has also been referred to as queen of the meadow, pride of the meadow, meadow-wort, meadow queen, lady of the meadow, dollof, meadsweet, and bridewort.
[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filipendula_ulmaria]"@en)
