AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_57919> "*Geum urbanum*, also known as wood avens, herb Bennet, colewort and St. Benedict's herb (Latin herba benedicta), is a perennial plant in the rose family (*Rosaceae*), which grows in shady places. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geum_urbanum]"@en)
