AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03303835> "Defined by Codex Alimentarius standard CODEX STAN 280-1973, Anhydrous milkfat is a milk product containing almost no water and non‑fat solids.  Anhydrous milk fat must contain at least 99.8 % milk fat and be made from fresh cream or butter. No additives are allowed, e.g. for neutralization of free fatty acids."@en)
