AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=292351>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4536>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> "Sheep Polypore"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> "Albatrellus ovinus (Schaeff.) Kotl. & Pouzar 1957")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> "Albatrellus ovinus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414536> "A terrestrial polypore fungus found in western North America, and Northern Europe. It is very closely related to the more common A. subrubescens, from which it may be distinguished microscopically by the amyloid spore wall."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=208468>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4537>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> "Caesar's mushroom"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> "Amanita caesarea (Scop.) Pers. 1801")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> "caesar's amanita"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414537> "A highly regarded edible mushroom in the genus Amanita, native to southern Europe and North Africa.

It has a distinctive orange cap, yellow gills and stipe. Similar orange-capped species occur in North America and India. It was known to and valued by the Ancient Romans, who called it Boletus, a name now applied to a very different type of fungus. First described by Giovanni Antonio Scopoli in 1772. [Wikipedia]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=309751>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4538>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> "pine bolete"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> "Boletus pinophilus Pilát & Dermek 1973")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414538> "A basidiomycete fungus of the genus Boletus found throughout Europe. The large, edible fruiting bodies known as mushrooms appear under pine trees, generally in summer and autumn.

It has a matte brown to maroon-coloured cap and its stem is often large and swollen, and the overall colour may have an orange-red tinge. As with other boletes, the size of the fruiting body is variable. Boletus pinophilus is edible, and may be preserved and cooked. [Wikipedia]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=200521>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4539>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> "Boletus aestivalis"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> "Boletus reticulatus Schaeff. 1774")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414539> "A basidiomycete fungus of the genus Boletus, occuring in deciduous forests of Europe where it forms a symbiotic mycorrhizal relationship with species of oak (Quercus). The fungus produces fruiting bodies in the summer months which are edible and popularly collected."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414540> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414540> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=327488>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414540> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4540>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414540> "Cantharellus pallens Pilát 1959")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414540> "A fungus often taken to be just a variety of Cantharellus cibarius var. pallens, but unlike \"true\" Cantharellus cibarius it yellows and then reddens when touched and has a weaker smell. Eyssartier and Roux classify it as a separate species but say that 90% of the chanterelles sold in French markets are this, not *Cantharellus cibarius*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=153130>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4541>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "trombetta dei morti"@it)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "trompette de la mort"@fr)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "trumpet of the dead"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "Craterellus cornucopioides (L.) Pers. 1825")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "Cantharellus cornucopioides"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414541> "An edible mushroom of genus Craterellus shaped like a horn."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=455453>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4543>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> "yellowfoot chanterelle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> "Craterellus tubaeformis (Fr.) Quél. 1888")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414543> "An edible fungus, smaller than the golden chanterelle (Cantharellus cibarius) and has a dark brown cap with paler gills and a hollow yellow stem.

\"It is mycorrhizal, forming symbiotic associations with plants, making it very challenging to cultivate. ... Craterellus tubaeformis tastes stronger but less fruity than the golden chanterelle. It has a very distinctive smokey, peppery taste when raw. \" - Wikipedia"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=356812>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4174>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4547>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> "bearded hedgehog mushroom"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> "monkey head mushroom"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> "satyr's beard"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> "Hericium erinaceus (Bull.) Pers. 1797")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414547> "An edible and medicinal mushroom belonging to the tooth fungus group. Native to North America, Europe and Asia it can be identified by its long spines (greater than 1 cm length), its appearance on hardwoods and its tendency to grow a single clump of dangling spines."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=225014>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4548>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> "Hydnum repandum L. 1753")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> "pied de mouton"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> "sweet tooth"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414548> "A basidiomycete fungus of genus Hydnum. The fungus produces fruit bodies (mushrooms) that are characterized by their spore-bearing structures—in the form of spines rather than gills—which hang down from the underside of the cap."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414549> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414549> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=219829>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414549> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4549>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414549> "Hydnum rufescens Pers. 1800")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414549> "An edible basidiomycete of the family Hydnaceae. It belongs to the small group of mushrooms often referred to as the tooth fungi, which produce fruit bodies whose cap undersurfaces are covered by hymenophores resembling spines or teeth, and not pores or gills."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414550> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414550> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=287857>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414550> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4550>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414550> "Macrolepiota procera (Scop.) Singer 1948")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414550> "A basidiomycete fungus with a large, prominent fruiting body resembling a parasol. It is a fairly common species on well-drained soils. It is found solitary or in groups and fairy rings in pastures and occasionally in woodland. Globally, it is widespread in temperate regions."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> "A species of fungus in the *Morchellaceae* family of the *Ascomycota*. It is one of the most readily recognized of all the edible mushrooms and highly sought after."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morchella_esculenta>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=247978>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4551>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414551> "Morchella esculenta (L.) Pers 1801")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> <http://www.indexfungorum.org/names/NamesRecord.asp?RecordID=303973>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B4552>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> "tamogitake"@jp)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> "Pleurotus citrinopileatus Singer 1942")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03414552> "An edible gilled fungus native to eastern Russia, northern China, and Japan, the golden oyster mushroom is very closely related to *Pleurotus cornucopiae* of Europe, with some authors considering them to be at the rank of subspecies."@en)
